# The C-BIOS build that nobasic-acceptance measures as the C-BIOS port's host (C-BIOS integration step 3,
# Joost 2026-11-27): the checkout's MSX1 EU build with NO BASIC, zerobas's disk ROM in slot 3-1.
# `tools/install_cbios_msx2.py --pinned` installs CBIOS2_CUR_MSX1_EU_NOBASIC_DISK from the copies in
# <openMSX share>/zerobas-cbios2/cur/ only when they hash to these; otherwise it is an INSTRUMENT FAULT, never green.
# To move the pin: build the new C-BIOS, `python3 tools/install_cbios_msx2.py --cbios <checkout>`, run
# `make nobasic-acceptance`, and update the revision and hashes below in the same commit.
# Measured 2026-11-27 (the same files as the checkout's derived/bin).
